record.content:
The relativistic total energy E of a particle is defined as 

\begin{equation}
E = \frac{mc^2}{\sqrt{1-v^2/c^2}}
\end{equation}

One often finds this relationship in the limit of low speeds $(v << c)$ with the famous equation

\begin{equation}
E_0 = mc^2
\end{equation}
